From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:27:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: clear recovery state before accepting new
 events

The full reset cleared hw_full_reset, which makes mt7915_reset() act on
firmware events again, before recovery.state and recovery.restart were
reset in mt7915_mac_reset_work(). An event in that window was then
overwritten, leaving MT76_MCU_RESET set with no recovery queued, and
all MCU commands failing from then on.

Reset state and restart first. Also make the recovery flags plain bools:
the irq tasklet and process context update them without a common lock,
and as bitfields in one byte an update could be lost.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/mac.c    | 9 ++++++---
 mt7915/mt7915.h | 9 ++++++---
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/mac.c b/mt7915/mac.c
index 1c7a36df..c5b37ee5 100644
--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -1518,6 +1518,12 @@ mt7915_mac_full_reset(struct mt7915_dev *dev)
 	dev->mt76.global_wcid.idx = i;
 	/* mt76_reset_device() unpublished it */
 	rcu_assign_pointer(dev->mt76.wcid[i], &dev->mt76.global_wcid);
+
+	/* everything signalled so far is handled by this reset, so clear it
+	 * before mt7915_reset() starts acting on new events again
+	 */
+	dev->recovery.state = MT_MCU_CMD_NORMAL_STATE;
+	dev->recovery.restart = false;
 	dev->recovery.hw_full_reset = false;
 
 	mutex_unlock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
@@ -1562,9 +1568,6 @@ void mt7915_mac_reset_work(struct work_struct *work)
 
 		/* enable WA/WM WDT */
 		mt76_set(dev, MT_WFDMA0_MCU_HOST_INT_ENA, MT_MCU_CMD_WDT_MASK);
-
-		dev->recovery.state = MT_MCU_CMD_NORMAL_STATE;
-		dev->recovery.restart = false;
 		return;
 	}
 
diff --git a/mt7915/mt7915.h b/mt7915/mt7915.h
index 7ee9bed8..4bc692bf 100644
--- a/mt7915/mt7915.h
+++ b/mt7915/mt7915.h
@@ -288,9 +288,12 @@ struct mt7915_dev {
 		u32 state;
 		u32 wa_reset_count;
 		u32 wm_reset_count;
-		bool hw_full_reset:1;
-		bool hw_init_done:1;
-		bool restart:1;
+		/* not bitfields: written from the irq tasklet and from
+		 * process context without a common lock
+		 */
+		bool hw_full_reset;
+		bool hw_init_done;
+		bool restart;
 	} recovery;
 
 	/* protects coredump data */
